WHAT THIS COVERS

  data/prints.csv        the published headline ledger
  data/series.csv        the published sub-series ledger
  data/panel/            the panels and how they were constructed
  data/agents/           the tracked crawler sets and their descriptions
  data/crawls/           which Common Crawl crawls make up the historical series
  data/raw/*/manifest.json
                         the observation manifests: what was requested, what
                         answered, and which stored body it produced

A suggested citation:

    Tallyhouse, Agent Accessibility Index, <period>.
    https://allanderek.github.io/tallyhouse/

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

  data/raw/bodies/       robots.txt files as published by third-party websites

Those files are other people's content. They are retained verbatim, and only
because an index that cannot be checked against its evidence is an assertion
rather than a measurement. No licence is granted over them here, and none could
be: they are not ours to license. Each remains subject to whatever rights its
publisher holds.

